IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpf-withdrawal`
IMPORT `cpf-medisave-and-contributions`

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953, ss 7, 16 and 25(1) -- worked cases.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `citizen or pr` IS A BOOLEAN, `over 55` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `credit` IS A NUMBER, `retirement sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Member
DECIDE `a member` `citizen or pr` `over 55` `credit` `retirement sum` IS
    Member WITH
        `name` IS "M"
        `a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore` IS `citizen or pr`
        `of a class prescribed under section 77(1) as an applicable person` IS FALSE
        `has attained the age of 55 years` IS `over 55`
        `has already withdrawn on the ground of having attained 55` IS FALSE
        `an anniversary of the date of birth has since passed, or the Minister has directed another period` IS FALSE
        `the sum standing to the member's credit` IS `credit`
        `the prescribed retirement sum applicable to the member` IS `retirement sum`
        `a reserved amount standing to the member's credit` IS 0

GIVEN `total` IS A NUMBER, `medisave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Accounts
DECIDE `accounts of` `total` `medisave` IS
    Accounts WITH
        `the total sum standing to the member's credit` IS `total`
        `the sum standing to the credit of the medisave account` IS `medisave`

GIVEN `member` IS A Member, `accounts` IS AN Accounts
GIVETH A MemberAccounts
DECIDE `a holding` `member` `accounts` IS
    MemberAccounts WITH
        `the member` IS `member`
        `the accounts` IS `accounts`
        `the Minister has approved a section 15AA(1) medisave withdrawal` IS FALSE

-- $200,000 in all, of which $60,000 is medisave; retirement sum $100,000.
`a citizen aged 60` MEANS `a member` TRUE TRUE 200000 100000
`a foreigner aged 40` MEANS `a member` FALSE FALSE 200000 100000
`the accounts` MEANS `accounts of` 200000 60000

§ `16 -- which routes can reach the medisave account`

#ASSERT NOT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15(2)(a) -- having attained 55` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15(3) -- the annual further withdrawal` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15(4) -- at the Board's discretion` FALSE

-- s 16(2): the s 15AA(1) route is barred EXCEPT with the Minister's approval.
#ASSERT NOT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15AA(1)` FALSE
#ASSERT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15AA(1)` TRUE

-- AND THE ROUTE s 16 DOES NOT NAME. s 16(1) restricts withdrawal "under section
-- 15(2)(a) or (3)". It says nothing about s 15(2)(b), the route for a member who
-- is not an applicable person. So the member who ceases to be a citizen or
-- permanent resident may take the medisave balance as well.
#ASSERT `the medisave account may be withdrawn by this route` `section 15(2)(b) -- not being an applicable person` FALSE

#ASSERT `the credit outside the medisave account` `the accounts` EQUALS 140000
#ASSERT `the sum this route can reach` `the accounts` `section 15(2)(a) -- having attained 55` FALSE EQUALS 140000
#ASSERT `the sum this route can reach` `the accounts` `section 15(2)(b) -- not being an applicable person` FALSE EQUALS 200000

§ `The correction to the first pass`

-- THE FIRST PASS WAS TOO HIGH. cpf-withdrawal.l4 computed the 55-year-old
-- citizen's entitlement on the whole credit and got $100,000: $200,000 less the
-- $100,000 retirement sum. s 16 takes the $60,000 medisave out of reach first,
-- so the real figure is $140,000 less $100,000 = $40,000.
#ASSERT `the amount this member may withdraw` `a citizen aged 60` TRUE EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the amount this member may actually withdraw` (`a holding` `a citizen aged 60` `the accounts`) TRUE EQUALS 40000

-- The two rules disagree by exactly the medisave balance, and that is the point
-- of keeping both: the older rule is what s 15 says on its own, and the newer
-- one is what s 15 and s 16 say together.

-- THE ASYMMETRY, SHARPENED. The member who stays loses both the retirement sum
-- and the medisave balance. The member who ceases to be an applicable person
-- loses neither and takes the whole $200,000.
#ASSERT `the amount this member may actually withdraw` (`a holding` `a foreigner aged 40` `the accounts`) TRUE EQUALS 200000

-- Where the non-medisave credit will not cover the retirement sum, nothing comes
-- out at all -- even though the member has $200,000 in the Fund.
`a citizen aged 60 with most of it in medisave` MEANS `a member` TRUE TRUE 200000 100000
`accounts mostly medisave` MEANS `accounts of` 200000 150000

#ASSERT `the credit outside the medisave account` `accounts mostly medisave` EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the amount this member may actually withdraw` (`a holding` `a citizen aged 60 with most of it in medisave` `accounts mostly medisave`) TRUE EQUALS 0

-- The Board's authority under s 15(1) is still required on top.
#ASSERT `the amount this member may actually withdraw` (`a holding` `a citizen aged 60` `the accounts`) FALSE EQUALS 0

-- A citizen under 55 is on no route at all.
`a citizen aged 40` MEANS `a member` TRUE FALSE 200000 100000
#ASSERT `the amount this member may actually withdraw` (`a holding` `a citizen aged 40` `the accounts`) TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `7 -- contributions`

GIVEN `rate` IS A NUMBER, `wages` IS A NUMBER, `interval` IS A NUMBER
    , `recovered` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ContributionFacts
DECIDE `contributions` `rate` `wages` `interval` `recovered` `paid in time` IS
    ContributionFacts WITH
        `the employer's contribution rate from the First Schedule` IS `rate`
        `the amount shown in the First Schedule as recoverable from the employee` IS 0
        `the employee's monthly wages` IS `wages`
        `the interval authorised by the Board, in months` IS `interval`
        `the employer recovered the employee's share from the wages` IS `recovered`
        `the employer paid the contributions to the Fund within the prescribed time` IS `paid in time`

#ASSERT `the contribution payable to the Fund` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 1480

-- s 7(1A): the Board may stretch the interval, but not beyond 6 months.
#ASSERT `the authorised interval is within section 7(1A)` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 6 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the authorised interval is within section 7(1A)` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 7 TRUE TRUE)

-- s 7(3) IS NARROWER THAN A GENERAL FAILURE-TO-PAY OFFENCE. It bites only where
-- the employer HAS ALREADY TAKEN the money out of the employee's wages. An
-- employer who never recovered the employee's share and never paid anything is
-- outside this subsection -- whatever other provisions may catch them.
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 1 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 1 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` (`contributions` 0.37 4000 1 TRUE TRUE)

-- Seven years' imprisonment for failing to hand over money already deducted
-- from an employee's wages -- the heaviest custodial maximum met anywhere in
-- this set of seven Acts.
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment under section 7(3) in years` EQUALS 7

§ `25(1) -- who may nominate`

#ASSERT `the member may make a nomination under section 25(1)` `a citizen aged 40` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the member may make a nomination under section 25(1)` `a citizen aged 40` FALSE

-- A MEMBER WHO IS NOT AN APPLICABLE PERSON MAY NOT NOMINATE, though they may
-- withdraw the entire Fund under s 15(2)(b). The Act lets them take everything
-- out and not say who should have it if they die first.
#ASSERT NOT `the member may make a nomination under section 25(1)` `a foreigner aged 40` TRUE
#ASSERT `the member is entitled to withdraw under section 15(2)(b)` `a foreigner aged 40`

§ `25(1)(a)(ii)(B) -- a large nomination is split in two`

-- Below the Minister's maximum, the whole portion goes into the nominee's own
-- CPF accounts.
#ASSERT `the amount transferred into the nominee's own accounts` 50000 80000 TRUE EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the amount paid out to the nominee` 50000 80000 TRUE EQUALS 0

-- Above it, the maximum is transferred and the excess is paid out.
#ASSERT `the amount transferred into the nominee's own accounts` 120000 80000 TRUE EQUALS 80000
#ASSERT `the amount paid out to the nominee` 120000 80000 TRUE EQUALS 40000

-- A nominee who is neither citizen nor permanent resident is paid the whole
-- portion in cash: there are no accounts to transfer it into.
#ASSERT `the amount transferred into the nominee's own accounts` 120000 80000 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount paid out to the nominee` 120000 80000 FALSE EQUALS 120000
